<title>USA: ALPINE SKIING-LEADING RESULTS IN MEN'S CUP SLALOM FIRST RUN.</title>
<headline>ALPINE SKIING-LEADING RESULTS IN MEN'S CUP SLALOM FIRST RUN.</headline>
<dateline>BRECKENRIDGE, Colorado 1996-12-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Leading</p>
<p>unofficial results in the first run of the men's World Cup</p>
<p>slalom at Breckenridge, Colorado, on Sunday:</p>
<p>1. Tom Stiansen (Norway) 51.75</p>
<p>2. Christiam Mayer (Austria) 51.82</p>
<p>3. Mario Reiter (Austria) 51.90</p>
<p>4. Jure Kosir (Sovenia) 52.04</p>
<p>5. Michael Von Gruenigen (Switzerland) 52.09</p>
<p>6. Thomas Sykora (Austria) 52.13</p>
<p>7. Kjetil Andre Aamodt (Norway) 52.16</p>
<p>8. Michael Tritscher (Austria) 52.33</p>
<p>9. Fredrik Nyberg (Sweden) 52.36</p>
<p>10. Sebastien Amiez (France) 52.30</p>
<p>:</p>
<p>The first-run results were later declared official.</p>
</text>
